A||||6||86SE||Whats this small black hose for??||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||03-04-2000||10:10 PM||||I looked at my EGR solenoid vaccume switch today and noticed a .25" to .5" in diameter black hose coming out of the back of it pointing towards the firewall!!  <BR>Anyways, I grabbed it and it was only about a foot long and not attached to anything!!  <BR>Is this hose supposed to be attached to anything??||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||03-04-2000||10:38 PM||||It is just the EGR filter vent hose, originally attached to a metal tube that runs across the back ot the firewall.  <BR>All other GM EGR solenoid designs that I have seen have no provisions for a filter vent hose, so I highly doubt that this hose/tube is even needed.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||b_b_a_d||03-05-2000||04:20 AM||||Mine is attached...  86 SE Automatic.<BR>I'll be back in a short while and post a photo if all goes well!<P>||||reg||3
Z||000003||AL||03-05-2000||04:37 AM||||that hose is there for one reason and that is for the switch to get good old fashion air, cold air if i'm right.so if you disconnect it will get hot air from the motor compartment,but all in all it shouldn't make a difference.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Luperman||03-05-2000||07:28 AM||||that hose goes to your egr valve connect it to the black metal tubing on the fire wall itself  then follow it along and you will see that is the one that actuates the egr valve itself <p>[This message has been edited by Luperman (edited 03-05-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||b_b_a_d||03-05-2000||08:46 AM||||I should clarify that the hose highlighted doesn't actually go into the EGR itself, it goes into the tube on the firewall <P>OK...  Here they are.  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/point01.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/point.jpg">  <P>Hope this helps a little.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 03-05-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Gokart||03-05-2000||06:42 PM||||When I had Cobra over a while back he noticed mine wasn't connected as well. He used a little grease to slip the hose back on to the metal tube along the firewall. Didn't really notice any difference and had my GT for at least 8 months back then and never had any codes, but figure it's gotta be there for a reason-so hook it up!||||reg||1
